  "created": "2026-10-21T08:23:56.747Z",
  "description": "Logi Plugin Tool is a command-line utility designed to assist developers in creating, building, packaging, verifying, and managing plugins for the Logi Actions SDK. Comprehensive SDK documentation is available at: https://logitech.github.io/actions-sdk-docs/",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "LogiPluginTool",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-21T08:29:55.257Z",
  "licenseUrl": "https://www.logitech.com/en-us/software/marketplace/developer-agreement.html",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "9PussXbS4FF8Rl9PYuq2RkY1IIkL0b8jq1WZGxwzbQs/WMsM81DCti5eWM2zu/ZtCdBklQNlDO2xwZy6JoPOPQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 34402924,
  "published": "2026-10-21T08:23:56.747Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Generated plugins now target .NET 10. They require Logi Plugin Service 6.4 or later at runtime.\n- Building a plugin no longer requires Logi Plugin Service to be installed. Generated plugins reference PluginApi through the `LogiPluginApi` NuGet package instead of `PluginApi.dll` from the Logi Plugin Service installation.\n- The `pack` command no longer bundles `PluginApi.dll` and its dependencies in the plugin package. Logi Plugin Service provides them at runtime.\n- Added the `devmode` command for viewing and changing developer mode.\n- The `verify` command can now validate Node.js plugins.\n- The `pack` command now adds `HasHapticMapping` to the package metadata when the plugin includes haptic event mappings. It previously added the misspelled `HasHapticsMapping`.",
  "repository": {
